{"claims":[{"claim":"Snippet behaviours (NameError without import, mutable default sharing, utcnow naive and deprecated, pandas != keeps missing, max of strings) match local runs.","source":"Local runs on CPython 3.13.12 and pandas 3.0.2, September 2026 (see D1, D3 and D5 claims).","status":"verified"}],"concept_html":"<p>This lesson is practice. Each exercise shows a short snippet in the style an assistant writes: tidy, plausible and typed. Each holds one seeded bug, drawn from your reference pipeline and from the lessons in Track D. The answer key stays hidden until you submit.</p>\n<p><strong>How to review each snippet:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Read the prompt's goal first. The bug is a gap between the goal and the code.</li>\n<li>Walk the lines in order. For each, ask: what does this assume, and what input breaks it?</li>\n<li>Tap the line you would change. Then write the fix, and run it against the checker.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>What to look for in Python and pandas code:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Names used but never imported, and imports that shadow built-ins.</li>\n<li>Deprecated calls: <code>datetime.utcnow()</code>, chained assignment, <code>applymap</code>.</li>\n<li>Type hints that lie: <code>str = None</code>.</li>\n<li>Truthiness where 0, 0.0 or an empty string is a valid value.</li>\n<li>Mutable default arguments.</li>\n<li>Joins that drop or duplicate rows, and nulls that behave unexpectedly in filters.</li>\n<li>Text compared where numbers were meant, such as wave ids.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your score counts two things: bugs found (the right line) and fixes proposed (a fix that passes the checker). Aim to find the bug before you open a hint. When a hint helps, note which one: that is the check you skipped.</p>\n<p>Work at your own pace. A snippet you get wrong is worth more than one you get right, as long as you read the explanation.</p>","example":{"language":"python","strong":{"lines":["<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">latest_wave</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">wave_ids</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">list</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">])</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>","<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"Return the most recent wave. Wave ids look like 'W' plus a number.\"\"\"</span>","    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"nb\">max</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">wave_ids</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"k\">lambda</span> <span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">int</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:]))</span>"],"notes":[{"html":"Compares the numbers, so W10 beats W9.","line":3}]},"takeaway_html":"<p>Goal first, then line by line: what does each line assume, and which input breaks it?</p>","weak":{"lines":["<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">latest_wave</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">wave_ids</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">list</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">])</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>","<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"Return the most recent wave.\"\"\"</span>","    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"nb\">max</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">wave_ids</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>"],"notes":[{"html":"Text comparison: max(['W9', 'W10']) is 'W9'.","line":3}]}},"exercises":[{"code":"def new_run_id() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return a new unique run id.\"\"\"\n    return str(uuid.uuid4())\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </sp